        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58324,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58325,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are superficially located within dermis and/or subcutaneous fat. The large majority of these lesions occur in the hands and feet {29957732; 29309308}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58326,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a small painless superficial tumour in acral sites.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58327,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a wide age range (1&ndash;68&nbsp;years), with female predilection {29957732; 29309308}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58328,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58329,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is defined by a fusion of exon&nbsp;7 of <em>EWSR1</em> with exon&nbsp;5 of <em>SMAD3</em> {29957732; 29309308}. SMAD3 is an important signal transducer in the TGF-&beta;/SMAD signalling pathway, which is involved in extracellular matrix synthesis by fibroblasts. By RNA sequencing, one case showed substantial upregulation of <em>FN1</em>, similar to other fibroblastic tumours, as well as ERG overexpression {29309308}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58330,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are small, measuring 1&ndash;2&nbsp;cm in greatest dimension, and have a nodular appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58331,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are typically well demarcated but show infiltration into subcutaneous fat. In particular in adult cases, the acellular centre of the tumour appears hyalinized, whereas the peripheral zones consist of intersecting cellular fascicles of fibroblastic spindle cells lacking nuclear pleomorphism, hyperchromasia, prominent nucleoli, or mitotic activity. Focally stippled dystrophic calcification may be found. By immunohistochemistry, the fibroblastic tumour cells consistently show diffuse ERG nuclear expression, whereas staining for SMA and CD34 is negative.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58332,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58333,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>SMAD3</em> fusion may be confirmed by molecular methods.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58334,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> small dermal and subcutaneous acral nodule; histological zonation with acellular hyalinized centre and peripheral fascicular spindle cell growth; immunoreactivity for ERG.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>EWSR1</em>-<em>SMAD3</em> fusion (if available).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58335,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58336,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>EWSR1</em>-<em>SMAD3</em>&ndash;positive fibroblastic tumour is benign. Local recurrence may occur after incomplete excision.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:19:43"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]